  "summary": "The consensus fix (replacing FeatureFile.list_all() with self._load_features(self.active_board) at lines 2093, 2137, and 2636) is correct and mechanically simple, but the discussion has overlooked a subtle sequencing issue in _periodic_server_push: it's a synchronous method (no async) calling _push_to_server which is async, meaning the await inside push_state may not execute as expected depending on how Textual's set_interval dispatches it — if _push_to_server is sometimes fire-and-forget rather than properly awaited, a second push could race the first and the server could still receive interleaved payloads. The three-line fix is necessary but the periodic push method should also be made async (or use call_later/run_worker) to ensure pushes are serialized. Additionally, the misleading comment at line 2634 should be removed as proposed, since it will otherwise invite a future contributor to 'fix' the filtered call back to an unfiltered one."
